   "path": "SCENE.md",
   "role": "instructions",
   "content": "# Gem Smoke\n\nSmoke in your palette flows behind and inside a glassy silhouette: a built-in shape such as a diamond, or a bold glyph or logo letter you type. Drawn in WebGL.\n\nCategory: shaders. Length: 5 s. WebGL: yes.\n\nUse when:\n- Brand or logo reveals that want smoke living inside and around a mark.\n- You have a short mark, letter or glyph to set in `glyph` and want it treated as a glassy silhouette.\n- A premium product intro wants color fields flowing through a recognizable shape.\n\nAvoid when:\n- You have no mark to show: the built-in shapes work, or use shader-smoke-ring or shader-neuro-noise for a shapeless field.\n- The mark should stay static and legible: the smoke will distort its read.\n- You need to feed a real logo image: this block draws text only.\n\nVariables:\n- speed (number, 0-4): Speed, default 1\n- colors (string): Colors, default \"#3a3a5c, #52527a\"\n- color_back (color): Background, default \"#0a0a10\"\n- color_inner (color): Inner color, default \"#fafaf5\"\n- shape (enum): Shape, default \"diamond\"\n- glyph (string): Glyph, default \"\"\n- inner_distortion (number, 0-1): Inner distortion, default 0.8\n- outer_distortion (number, 0-1): Outer distortion, default 0.6\n- outer_glow (number, 0-1): Outer glow, default 0.55\n- inner_glow (number, 0-1): Inner glow, default 1\n- size (number, 0-1): Smoke size, default 0.8\n- offset (number, -1-1): Offset, default 0\n- angle (number, 0-360): Angle, default 0\n- rotation (number, 0-360): Rotation, default 0\n- scale (number, 0.1-4): Scale, default 0.6\n- resolution (number, 0.25-1): Resolution, default 0.5\n\nSource: https://github.com/Remocn/remocn. Licence: MIT. The scene file keeps the upstream notice.\n"
  },
